.Dd November 23, 2026
.Dt CUDA-OBJDUMP 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cuda-objdump
.Nd list the members of a cuda-native fatbin container
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -json | Fl -jsonl
.Ar file
.Nm
.Fl -extract
.Ar index output
.Ar file
.Nm
.Fl -schema
.Nm
.Fl -version
.Op Fl -json
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
lists the members of a cuda-native fatbin container.
The container is LLVM's
.Em OffloadBinary
format, version 2; see
.Xr nvfatbin 5 .
.Pp
.Ar file
is either the container itself or an ELF object or executable that carries
one in its
.Pa .nv_fatbin
section, which is where clang puts it.
When the file is an ELF object, the container is read from that section.
.Pp
Without an output option
.Nm
prints one line per member:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
file.fatbin: container, container version 2, 2 members
[0] ptx arch=sm_120 format=ptx size=78 sha256=HASH sha256_ok=yes
[1] ptx arch=sm_121a format=ptx size=80 sha256=HASH sha256_ok=yes
.Ed
.Pp
A member whose container carries no
.Dv cloudbsd.format
or
.Dv cloudbsd.sha256
key shows a dash for that field.
.Pp
.Fl -json
prints one JSON document that holds every member.
.Fl -jsonl
prints a header line and then one line per member, and flushes every line
as it is written, so a reader that stops early ends the program cleanly.
.Pp
Only one output mode may be given.
.Nm
refuses
.Fl -json
and
.Fl -jsonl
together, refuses
.Fl -extract
with either of them, and refuses a second
.Fl -extract ;
each refusal names the options that cannot be combined, and the exit status
is 2.
.Pp
The path and the metadata of the members come from outside the tool.
The text output shows every control byte as a
.Ql \exNN
escape, so no raw control byte reaches the terminal and one member stays
one line.
The JSON output writes every byte that is not a UTF-8 character as the
replacement character, so the document is always valid UTF-8 JSON.
.Pp
A file that cannot be read says why: it is not there, the permission is
refused, the input is a directory, the input is empty, the read failed, or
the host is out of memory.
.Pp
The JSON output validates against
.Pa share/cuda-native/schema/cuda-objdump-1.schema.json ,
which
.Nm
also prints with
.Fl -schema .
.Pp
.Fl -extract
.Ar index output
writes the image of member
.Ar index
to the file
.Ar output
and prints nothing.
.Pp
.Fl 64
and
.Fl g
are not accepted; the tool has no options of its own beyond those above.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--extract index output"
.It Fl -json
Print one JSON document instead of text.
.It Fl -jsonl
Print a header line and one line per member.
.It Fl -extract Ar index output
Write the image of member
.Ar index
to
.Ar output .
.Ar index
is a non-negative decimal number, and anything else is a usage problem.
For a number that names no member the diagnostic says which indexes the
container has.
.It Fl -schema
Print the JSON schema of this tool's output.
.It Fl -version
Print the version of the tool.
With
.Fl -json
it prints one JSON object.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print usage.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
In detail, exit status 0 means the container was read, 2 reports a usage
problem and 1 reports a file that is not a readable container, a container
that fails a check, or an output that cannot be written.
.Sh EXAMPLES
List the members of a container:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
cuda-objdump kernel.fatbin
.Ed
.Pp
Print one JSON document and take the first member out of it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
cuda-objdump --json kernel.fatbin
cuda-objdump --extract 0 kernel.ptx kernel.fatbin
.Ed
.Pp
List the container clang put in an object file:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
cuda-objdump kernel.o
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nvfatbin 1 ,
.Xr nvptxas 1 ,
.Xr libcudart-stub 3 ,
.Xr nvfatbin 5 ,
.Xr cuda-native-toolchain 7
.Sh CAVEATS
The tool reads a cuda-native container only.
It never reads an NVIDIA fatbinary, and it does not execute or assemble any
device code.
